"""RED GARDEN — the arena MOBA (apps/arena) and its server/matchmaker/bot binaries, under Bazel.

Founder real-time: "i want the bazel migration done now" (S202-36). Replaces
scripts/build.sh, scripts/build_arena.sh, scripts/test_arena.sh, and
scripts/build_training.sh as the primary build entry point, following the
same real precedent PARENA's own MODULE.bazel/BUILD.bazel setup already
established in this monorepo -- not a new pattern invented here.

Real motivation beyond "the founder asked": build_arena.sh was a second,
fully redundant copy of build.sh's own apps/arena target -- REDGARDEN hit
the exact same "a new PARENA mod lands, gets wired into most build paths,
gets missed in one" bug class at least three separate times this session
alone (bloodflower_mod, tree_passive_mod, abraham_fireball_mod each missing
from one shell script or ci.yml's own Windows step at some point). A real
dependency graph, where a binary depends on a library and that library's
own srcs list is the single source of truth, makes that whole bug class
structurally impossible -- not "remember to check five files," one file.

No external dependencies beyond rules_cc -- this repo's own C code has no
third-party library deps of its own (SDL2/OpenGL are system libraries,
linked via linkopts, not fetched by Bazel).
"""

module(
    name = "redgarden",
    version = "0.0.0",
)

bazel_dep(name = "rules_cc", version = "0.2.17")
